The small eligible forward slice is now excluded directly in the full
point-core branch above distance four. A conjugated seed realizes all of
R₃; its transported reverse kernel controls the entire shifted span modulo
the center seed, forcing it into the center two-core and making R₃ trivial.
This proves the strict index and supplies the actual backward critical
shift without the intermediate second-local-group centrality argument.
The bound also transports to every critical walk. Iterating the actual backward
shift now preserves every overlap and constructs a critical walk beginning
