The full forward-kernel vanishing criterion now covers both critical image
sizes. Every eligible small slice has a noncentral order-two line, and the
large-image branch constructs the actual shifted endpoint and residual
conjugator without point-core equality. In the full point-core branch a
small forward slice also supplies a small critical pair elsewhere, giving
rank-one transpositions on the entire seed. In the full point-core branch, fixed full-seed vectors now have duad
orbits. Their centralizers generate with any escaping actor, so the
large-image restricted actor proves forward-line centrality and the
