opposite-core control and the terminal contradiction are still required.
The remaining strict reciprocal slice now supplies a moving central
involution outside the opposite Baumann slice, on the same selected path.
Both moving subgroups have index at most two modulo the opposite full
radius centers. Transport to the base vertex forces nontrivial component
movement of Omega_1 Z(V_alpha) modulo Z_alpha, distinct from X_alpha.
This movement now forces at least two noncentral factors in the literal
radius quotient. Otherwise the unique-factor dichotomy and abelian edge
generation would make the radius abelian, contrary to the selected line.
Every actor containing an even involution in the original symmetric image
therefore has fixed index at least sixteen on that quotient. The actual
whole-core and C.1.32 consumers retain both covers and the plane/Sylow
alternatives. Excluding this obstruction, the other radical branches and
independent natural exhaustion remains necessary for both reconstructions.
In the point-core branch every transposition actor now has fixed index at
least four on the full radius quotient. The whole-radius midpoint kernel
therefore moves the opposite full critical kernel nontrivially. It produces
