radii on every critical path. The shifted-seed comparison in MS93 (5.12),
including its distinct X endpoint, remains necessary to exclude this line.
The point-core branch now forces central generation of every full omega
layer. A generating backward edge makes its shifted kernel line central
at the original vertex; the noncentral-extension control bound would force
a small moving slice, contradicting the proved strict reciprocal slice.
Thus X_a = U_a C_{X_a}(G_a) and X_a = Z_a on this original graph. The same
selected span retains its central derived line, and its shifted kernel
commutator lies in both midpoint seeds and centralizes the original
stabilizer. The central-generation case of the remaining commutator bound,
